From 44956c778bf973de8beba846d31ce2f2f8e869c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Skowron <1019893+Cinderella-Man@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:13:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] CUDA: bound the rows of mul_mat_vec_q by nrows_x, not
 stride_col_dst

The write guard and the bias prefetch of mul_mat_vec_q let a row through
while row0 + i < stride_col_dst (#25445, #16847). For MUL_MAT_ID with one
token, dst holds the used experts' outputs next to each other and
stride_col_dst is nrows_x * n_used. When nrows_x is not a multiple of the
block's rows (4 with a small K, 2 for the low-bit types of
mmvq_two_rows_ncols1), the last block of each slot writes its rows past
nrows_x, computed from the memory after its expert's matrix, over the first
rows of the next slot, racing with that slot's own first block. The last
slot writes past the end of dst, and the bias prefetch reads past the
expert's bias.

Pass nrows_x to the kernel and bound by it, as mul_mat_vec_q_moe already
does. nrows_x <= stride_col_dst on every launch, and rows at or past nrows_x
exist only when nrows_x is not a multiple of the block's rows, so every
other shape gives the same output as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
